    "content": "{\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Improve memory locality and loop order by reorganizing the loops to process points in a more cache-friendly manner. Specifically, we will focus on reducing the number of times distances are updated and sorted by using blocking techniques.\",\n    \"transformations\": [\n        \"Reorganized the nested loops to improve cache locality by processing blocks of points together.\",\n        \"Reduced the frequency of sorting operations by maintaining a fixed-size list of nearest neighbors.\"\n    ],\n    \"sources_kept\": [],\n    \"files\": [\n        {\n            \"path\": \"src/knn.c\",\n            \"content\": \"#include \\\"knn.h\\\"\\n\\n#define BLOCK_SIZE 16\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n    float distance;\\n    char label;\\n} Neighbor;\\n\\nint compare_neighbors(const void *a, const void *b) {\\n    Neighbor *da = (Neighbor *)a;\\n    Neighbor *db = (Neighbor *)b;\\n    return (da->distance > db->distance) - (da->distance < db->distance);\\n}\\n\\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group *groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\\n    Neighbor neighbors[k];\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\\n        neighbors[i].distance = -1;\\n        neighbors[i].label = -1;\\n    }\\n\\n    for (int block_i = 0; block_i < n_groups; block_i += BLOCK_SIZE) {\\n        int end_i = (block_i + BLOCK_SIZE > n_groups) ? n_groups : block_i + BLOCK_SIZE;\\n        for (int i = block_i; i < end_i; i++) {\\n            Group g = groups[i];\\n\\n            for (int block_j = 0; block_j < g.length; block_j += BLOCK_SIZE) {\\n                int end_j = (block_j + BLOCK_SIZE > g.length) ? g.length : block_j + BLOCK_SIZE;\\n                for (int j = block_j; j < end_j; j++) {\\n                    float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, g.points[j]);\\n\\n                    if (d < neighbors[k - 1].distance || neighbors[k - 1].distance == -1) {\\n                        neighbors[k - 1].distance = d;\\n                        neighbors[k - 1].label = g.label;\\n\\n                        qsort(neighbors, k, sizeof(Neighbor), compare_neighbors);\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    char most_frequent = neighbors[0].label;\\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\\n    int current_frequency = 1;\\n\\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; i++) {\\n        if (neighbors[i].label != neighbors[i - 1].label) {\\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\\n                most_frequent = neighbors[i - 1].label;\\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\\n            }\\n\\n            current_frequency = 1;\\n        } else {\\n            current_frequency++;\\n        }\\n\\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\\n            most_frequent = neighbors[i].label;\\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    return most_frequent;\\n}\\n\\nint main() {\\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\\n    \\n    Group *groups = (Group *)malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\\n    }\\n\\n    int k = parse_k();\\n\\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\\n\\n    printf(\\\"%c\\\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\\n}\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"path\": \"src/knn.h\",\n            \"content\": \"#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n\\n#define BLOCK_SIZE 16\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n    float x;\\n    float y;\\n} Point;\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n    char label;\\n    int length;\\n    Point *points;\\n} Group;\\n\\nvoid on_error() {\\n    printf(\\\"Invalid input file.\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(1);\\n}\\n\\nint parse_number_of_groups() {\\n    int n;\\n    if (scanf(\\\" n_groups=%d \\\", &n) != 1) on_error();\\n\\n    return n;\\n}\\n\\nPoint parse_point() {\\n    float x, y;\\n    if (scanf(\\\" (%f ,%f) \\\", &x, &y) != 2)  on_error();\\n\\n    Point point;\\n    point.x = x;\\n    point.y = y;\\n\\n    return point;\\n}\\n\\nGroup parse_next_group() {\\n    char label; \\n    int length;\\n\\n    if (scanf(\\\" label=%c \\\", &label) != 1) on_error();\\n    if (scanf(\\\" length=%d \\\", &length) != 1) on_error();\\n\\n    Group group;\\n    group.label = label;\\n    group.length = length;\\n    group.points = (Point *)malloc(sizeof(Point) * length);\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {\\n        group.points[i] = parse_point();\\n    }\\n\\n    return group;\\n}\\n\\nint parse_k() {\\n    int k;\\n    if (scanf(\\\" k=%d \\\", &k) != 1) on_error();\\n\\n    return k;\\n}\\n\\nfloat euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(Point a, Point b) {\\n    float dx = b.x - a.x;\\n    float dy = b.y - a.y;\\n    return dx * dx + dy * dy;\\n}\\n\\nint compare_for_sort(const void *a, const void *b) {\\n  Neighbor *da = (Neighbor *)a;\\n  Neighbor *db = (Neighbor *)b;\\n  return (da->distance > db->distance) - (da->distance < db->distance);\\n}\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"notes\": \"Reorganized the nested loops to improve cache locality by processing blocks of points together. Reduced the frequency of sorting operations by maintaining a fixed-size list of nearest neighbors.\"\n}"
